expr main [weather, wether, wheather] or not
let message "Use `whether` to introduce a choice between alternatives. `Weather` refers to atmospheric conditions."
let description "Corrects `weather or not` (and similar misspellings) to `whether or not`."
let becomes "whether or not"

test "I don't know weather or not it will work." "I don't know whether or not it will work."
test "She asked wether or not we were coming." "She asked whether or not we were coming."
test "Weather or not we go depends on the schedule." "Whether or not we go depends on the schedule."
test "I don't know whether or not it will work." "I don't know whether or not it will work."
test "The weather is nice, or not." "The weather is nice, or not."
